  "notes": "Result: 10 rows audited, 10 correct, 0 imprecise, 0 wrong. Method: static reading only at commit 7eddde7895 plus the staged files. No build, test or script was run. Each sample row is identical to its row in README.env-vars.md (checked by exact line match). Every row is at or under 1,000 characters (largest: UV_VERSION, 989 characters). The points below are omissions that I did not count as problems. They do not change what a reader would do. (1) VALIDATE_TOKENIZERS says the mode uses ids that it picks itself. The code takes bos_token_id and eos_token_id from tokenizer_config.json, then from config.json, and falls back to 128000 and 128001 (src/rinzler/tokenizers.cpp:1941-1974). The row has 973 characters, so there is little room for this. (2) VALIDATE_TOKENIZERS lists rinzler, runtron and rinzler_proxy. rinzler_mock and rinzler_host are also built from src/rinzler.cpp and read it the same way (src/CMakeLists.txt:115, 152). (3) IN_NIX_SHELL has 'Reads and sets' in the Tron cell. Test scripts under bin/ci also remove it for child processes (for example bin/ci/test-make-environment-guidance.sh:32). (4) SLICE_STATE_DIR: an empty value also gives /tmp (bin/slice:92). That equals the unset case, so the row needs no 'Empty:' text. bin/slice queue reads the state files only when shared Dice routing is active (bin/slice:6020-6034). (5) TRON_MIN_MAIN_HELPERS: a pass can leave no attention worker only when TRON_MAX_MAIN_HELPERS is also set to the pool size or more, because the minimum is capped by the maximum (h/tron/models/model.hpp:2414). The row does not contradict this."
